From: yugidraft <yugidraft@localhost>
Date: Thu, 3 Feb 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: player-effect side, unique cards and summon-to-opponent
 procedures for more than two duelists

The stock code uses effect_owner, controler ^ p and opponent_of at three more sites.
With more than 2 duelists these gave the wrong side, or seat 255.
Every change is in an n_duelists > 2 branch. The n == 2 text is unchanged.

effect.cpp, effect::is_target_player: the own side of an ABSOLUTE_TARGET effect is get_owner_player().
effect_owner is none_id() for effects that a startup script made, so no seat matched it.
In a team game the own side is still team 0.

card.cpp, card::get_unique_target: the own side is the controller.
The other side is every living duelist that is not on the team of the controller.
The partner in a team game is not an opponent. A dead duelist is not looked at.
This is the same rule that field::add_unique_card already uses.

card.cpp, check_summon_procedure, check_set_procedure, filter_spsummon_procedure:
a procedure with EFFECT_FLAG_SPSUM_PARAM and an o_range means "to the field of an opponent".
With more than 2 duelists the check passes when at least one living opponent works.
The opponents are tried clockwise from the player. The first one that works is the target.
If none works, the procedure is not allowed. There is no trap and no read out of range.
A small helper, opponents_in_turn_order, lists the living opponents.

Left alone: the zone swaps in card.cpp. They are pure bit math with no seat.
Still open in operations.cpp (other task): the "1 - sumplayer" and "1 - setplayer" lines and the zone swaps.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
